meta {
  name: SystemUserPackageRequest
  seq: 10
}

auth {
  mode: inherit
}

docs {
  Feature: System users send access package requests to organisations

    A system user owned by a public sector organisation (KOMM, FYLK or STAT) can ask an
    organisation, identified by organisation number, for an access package through
    POST /accessmanagement/api/v1/systemuser/request/package. The token is a system user
    token carrying the scope altinn:accessmanagement/systemuser:requests.write; the consumer
    claim identifies the organisation that owns the system user.

    A system user can never receive requests, and system users owned by any other kind of
    organisation are rejected.

  Personas and seed data live in testdata/<tokenEnv>.js next to this file:
    - publicSectorConsumer: KOMM/FYLK/STAT organisation that owns systemUser
    - privateConsumer: organisation of another type that owns privateSystemUser
    - recipient: organisation receiving the request, with its dagligleder
    - package: an access package the recipient can grant

  Requires the EnableSystemUserRequests feature flag in the target environment.
}
